# Build output
#
# The binary patterns below MUST stay anchored with a leading slash. An
# unanchored `shellforge` matches any path component with that name at any
# depth, which silently excluded the entire cmd/shellforge package directory
# from the repository: `git ls-files cmd/shellforge/` returned nothing, and
# because CI builds with `go build ./...` and tests with `go test ./...`, both
# skipped a package that was not there and reported green. The CLI entry point
# was untracked from Day 0 until issue #11 found it.
/bin/
/dist/
/build/
/shellforge
/shellforge.exe
# cmd/sf-ptyhost builds to the repo root by default, and it is a linux
# binary rather than a .exe, so nothing above catches it. It reached main
# once that way: 2.9 MB of unstripped ELF in commit 8fd9dc1. `make ptyhost`
# writes it to images/out/bin/, which /images/out/ below already covers.
/sf-ptyhost
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Never commit sandbox artifacts. A rootfs tarball is 40-120 MB and a vhdx is 2 GB.
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.vhdx
/images/out/
/rootfs*

# Local progress and state
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
/state/
/.shellforge/

# Go
/vendor/
go.work
go.work.sum
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.prof
/testdata/tmp/

# Python. Only the CI gate checker and its tests are Python, but pytest leaves
# bytecode caches next to them and they must never be committed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Secrets. Nothing in this project should need one, which is why an accidental
# commit would be worth catching.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Scratch
/tmp/
/scratch/
*.log
!packs/**/assets/*.log
